WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.800
Nice beard.

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.080
Help!

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:03.680
I am help!

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:05.200
I'm Maeve's friend.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.200
He is her complicated
love interest.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:08.280
I love you.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.560
Oatcake, you alright?

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:20.120
I'm A-OK, Eric.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.920
I'm fine. I'm chillaxed!

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:24.080
To the max!

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:26.920
OK then, Mr Moustache.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.280
So you guys didn't speak
much over summer?

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:30.280
No.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.880
And I haven't heard
from him since last term.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:34.840
I always thought
you two would make up.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:36.640
We're not fighting.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:37.920
We're just not
friends anymore.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.000
An on-campus sex clinic
for teenagers is

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.560
rather entrepreneurial,
in my opinion.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.840
It shows a lot
of business savvy.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.400
We don't run
the clinic anymore.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:51.560
We've realised,
it wasn't very ethical.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:53.600
-And we--
-We stopped being friends.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:55.640
We grew apart.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.880
Oh. That's a shame.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:00.120
So why aren't
we friends anymore?

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:03.680
Nice beard.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.320
What's your point?

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.200
Nothing.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:12.960
We're just
in very different places.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:15.920
It's called a moustache.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:18.400
Yeah, no shit.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:20.840
We need to tell Hope
she can't teach this stuff.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:21.840
It's backwards.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:23.680
She's not gonna listen.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:25.440
We need to do something.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:26.960
Like what?

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:28.120
I don't know.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.520
Maybe we could help people,
like before.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:33.200
You mean take their money?

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.880
That wasn't the only thing
the clinic was about, Otis.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.440
What else was it about?

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.040
I'm not getting
involved anymore.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:42.920
It's not my problem.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.080
It's not your problem?

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.880
Why?

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.840
Because you're too cool now?
You don't need to care?

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.880
You didn't want to do
the clinic either, Maeve.

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:53.680
Yeah, you're right.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:54.840
And now I remember why.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:56.120
I'm going to the library.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.160
This trip is the worst.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:01.960
Can't get much worse
than a rogue poo.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:08.360
Where's the coach?

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:11.960
It's getting dark.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:14.360
It's gonna be cold
once it's dark.

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:16.840
I'm panicking.
Are you panicking?

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.960
No, we're not gonna
starve to death, Otis.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:21.440
I don't think you're taking
this seriously, Maeve.

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:23.480
-We could die.
-We're not gonna die!

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.360
Someone will drive past
and we can use their phone.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.400
-It's gonna be fine.
-We should hitchhike.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.600
OK.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:31.240
How do you say "help"
in French?

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:32.400
How do I say "help"?

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.160
Help!

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.800
I am help!

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:41.920
Why are you laughing?

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.040
Sorry. You're just really
funny when you're stressed.

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:45.600
Well, you're
not helping, Maeve.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:47.800
What did it say…

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:51.360
the voicemail?

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.000
Doesn't matter.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:55.880
It was ages ago.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.200
Matters to me.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.320
It was something like…

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.560
"Hi, Maeve."

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:10.120
"I'm watching you
on TV right now."

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:16.560
"And I wanted to let you
know how proud I am of you."

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.240
"And about how you saying
you had feelings for me

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:24.760
was all I ever
wanted to hear…

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:27.800
because
it's always been you."

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:32.240
"I love you."

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:36.760
I mean, anyway,
it was stupid.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:39.080
Did you mean it?

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:43.240
Of course I meant it.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:01.840
I can't-- I can't do this.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:02.920
OK.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:04.640
I understand.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:14.920
I don't--

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.440
I don't wanna
lose you again.

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:19.400
I know. I'm confused.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:20.640
This is confusing me.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:39.520
Oh, Milburn,

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:40.920
you're here, too.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.600
We had no idea
you were missing.

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:44.400
So sorry.

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:45.920
Come on, guys, on the coach.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.080
On the coach!

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.360
Maeve.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:54.360
Yeah?

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:57.640
We should talk
about what happened.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:00.880
Is it OK
if we don't tonight?

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.400
I need to sort my head out.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:06.080
That's OK.

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:19.200
I'm sorry.

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:24.000
I just wasn't expecting

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:26.680
what happened
between us to happen.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:29.800
-Yeah.
-And, um…

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:32.560
I like Isaac.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.000
You know, I think
we have something good.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:39.960
OK, I'll meet them there.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:42.320
You OK?

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.640
No. I need to go to Anna's.
There's an emergency.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:48.240
OK.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:50.000
-Do you want my bike?
-No.

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:52.040
-It's quicker.
-I can't ride a bike, Otis.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.240
-What do you mean?
-I can't.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:54.800
No one ever
fucking taught me, OK?

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:56.600
The police are here.

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:02.760
-Hi.
-Hi.

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:05.120
I wanted to make sure
you were OK.

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:06.160
Thank you.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:10.400
-What are you doing here?
-She needed a lift.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:12.680
That's convenient.

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:15.360
-And what about buses?
-We thought about buses too.

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:16.720
And you can tap her phone.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:19.440
Sorry. How are you both
connected to the case again?

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:20.920
I'm Maeve's friend.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.040
He is her complicated
love interest.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:24.440
You used to be her friend

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:26.280
until you were an arsehole
at that party.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:27.920
I think
the only arsehole here

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:29.240
is the man
who deleted my voicemail

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:30.280
without telling her--

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:31.880
Right. Outside, both of you.

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:35.000
Outside.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:36.320
-Yep.
-OK.

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:39.800
You're always popping up
where people don't want you.

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:41.360
-Just go home.
-You don't know me.

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:42.800
You're always
making things worse.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:44.160
What are you
even doing here--

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:47.400
Shut up, the pair of you!
My sister is missing.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:48.680
This is not
an opportunity for you

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:49.880
to swing your dicks around.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:52.200
I don't know how you could
think of choosing this guy.

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:53.880
Choosing? What are you
talking about "choosing"?

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:55.320
You're so deluded.

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:03.120
Oh, right.

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:06.680
Something happened between
you guys on the trip then?

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:10.400
Ye-- Yeah.

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:13.440
Look, it doesn't
mean anything.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.480
I mean, I…
I don't know what it means.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:17.640
It's just, Elsie's missing.

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:19.000
That's all I care
about right now.

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:22.440
Well, good luck
finding her, Maeve.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:24.160
Isaac, don't go.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:27.720
Fuck.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:28.960
Thanks, Otis.

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:30.680
I think
I should stay and help.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:32.640
No, I don't think so.
You make things worse.

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:34.640
What do you mean?

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:35.600
Since stopping the clinic,

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:37.160
you stopped caring
about anyone but yourself.

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:38.360
No, that's not true.

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:41.600
It's just
not my responsibility.

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:43.160
I think you should go.

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:45.080
I don't wanna
see you anymore.

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:46.200
Maeve.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.320
It was never
about the clinic.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:51.360
I did the clinic
to be close to you.

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:55.480
And then you made me realise
I'm good at something.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:57.640
And I like helping people.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:00.720
And I thought
you ignored my message

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:02.240
and it crushed my heart.

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:04.680
I stopped the clinic because
it reminded me of you

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:05.720
and it sucked.

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:08.600
So I wanna help people.

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:12.600
And I know this is only
about money for you,

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:16.240
but let's just
be a team again, please.

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:17.880
If I can't be with you
romantically,

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:19.520
I still wanna
see you every day.

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:22.680
Nothing feels right
when you're not around.

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:25.520
It wasn't just
about the money for me.

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:29.040
I wanted to be close
to you too.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:03.800
-Maeve!
-Good morning.

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:04.920
Good-- Oh, my--

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:07.360
Good morning. Oh, my God.

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:12.040
What are we gonna do today?

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:15.640
Hey.

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:19.080
What are you doing here?

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:26.040
OK.

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:28.720
I've changed my mind.

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:31.440
About what?

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:32.440
America.

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:36.240
I found the money,
so I'm going.

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:37.600
Right.

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:39.400
When?

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:41.640
Now.

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:43.760
Wow.

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:46.080
-Yeah.
-Oh.

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:51.080
You know you don't need
my help with the clinic?

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:52.440
It's your gift.

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:53.760
Yeah, and what about us?

00:09:55.480 --> 00:09:57.040
We'll have to see where
we're at when I'm back.

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:08.480
I'm proud of you.

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:10.800
I mean it.

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:13.920
-America.
-Yeah.

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:20.680
So this is goodbye.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:21.720
No.

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:23.440
No.

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:26.400
It's "see you soon."

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:41.560
OK, cool. Wish me luck.

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:42.920
OK.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:44.320
Bye, Eric.

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:46.080
Bye, Maeve.

